  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "- **`IMutex.Global` is shared by every user's processes on Unix again, as its documentation says.** Since .NET 11, and 8.0.32, 9.0.21 and 10.0.13, .NET scopes a named mutex on Unix to its user unless told otherwise, so processes of different users each had a mutex of their own. Every process that shares a global mutex on Unix must use this version or a later one: an earlier one's mutex is its user's own. Its documentation now repeats .NET's warning that on Unix such a mutex should be shared only between users who trust each other.",
